.TH 6ix9ine 1 "July 2026" "6ix9ine v1.0.0" "6ix9ine CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
6ix9ine \- keeps your Mac awake only while work is happening, then lets it sleep
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 6ix9ine
[\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-h\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B 6ix9ine
is a background utility that monitors active work sessions from AI agents and other processes, keeping your macOS system awake (even in closed-lid clamshell mode on docked Macs) while tasks are running, and automatically restoring normal sleep behavior as soon as all sessions complete.
It acts as a reference-counted sleep-blocking controller using a three-tier model: client hooks/commands, a user-level policy daemon, and a minimal root-privileged sleep helper.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B acquire \fIsession_id\fR [\fB\-\-tool\fR \fItool_name\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR \fIreason\fR]
Acquire a sleep-blocking session. Increments the reference count.
.TP
.B release \fIsession_id\fR
Release a sleep-blocking session. Decrements the reference count.
.TP
.B hold \fIsession_id\fR \fIduration\fR [\fB\-\-tool\fR \fItool_name\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR \fIreason\fR]
Acquire a session with a temporary timed hold (e.g., "30m", "1h20m", or seconds).
.TP
.B track \fIpid\fR [\fB\-\-tool\fR \fItool_name\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR \fIreason\fR]
Track a specific PID. The sleep block will automatically be released when the process terminates.
.TP
.B status
Print the current active sessions, sleep blocking state, lid position, and thermal readings.
.TP
.B install\-hooks [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\fR \fIagent_name\fR]
Install agent lifecycle hooks to auto-trigger sleep blocking (e.g., Claude Code, OpenCode).
.TP
.B uninstall\-hooks [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\fR \fIagent_name\fR]
Remove agent lifecycle hooks.
.TP
.B setup\-privileged\-helper
Install the root LaunchDaemon helper tool which handles low-level sleep blocking. Requires administrative privileges (sudo).
.TP
.B helper\-status
Verify that the root-privileged helper LaunchDaemon is running and responsive.
.TP
.B uninstall\-helper
Unload and remove the privileged helper LaunchDaemon. Requires administrative privileges (sudo).
.TP
.B daemon\-start
Load and start the user-level background daemon LaunchAgent.
.TP
.B daemon\-stop
Stop and unload the user-level background daemon LaunchAgent.
.TP
.B daemon\-restart
Restart the user-level background daemon LaunchAgent.
.TP
.B daemon\-status
Check if the user-level background daemon is running and retrieve its socket status.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version string and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SIXNINE_STATE_DIR
Override the default directory for runtime sockets and state files (defaults to \fI~/Library/Application Support/6ix9ine\fR).
.TP
.B SIXNINE_THERMAL_THRESHOLD
Specify the CPU temperature threshold in degrees Celsius (default: 85) at which sleep blocking is aborted to protect hardware.
.TP
.B SIXNINE_IDLE_TIMEOUT
Idle timeout in minutes (default: 5) after which sleep blocking is automatically released if no CPU activity is detected.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start a manual hold for 45 minutes:
.IP
.B 6ix9ine hold my-build 45m --tool manual --reason "compiling source code"
.PP
Track an active background task with process ID 12345:
.IP
.B 6ix9ine track 12345 --tool manual --reason "running overnight migrations"
.PP
Check daemon and helper status:
.IP
.B 6ix9ine status
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
If the daemon is offline, start it with:
.IP
.B 6ix9ine daemon-start
.PP
If you encounter "Permission denied" errors during setup, ensure you run:
.IP
.B 6ix9ine setup-privileged-helper
with an admin account. You will be prompted for your macOS password.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR t69 (1),
.BR pmset (1)
